# Prep Meal Theme Rules

## Content architecture
- Every content section supports **Metaobject list** mode and **blocks fallback**.
- If a `metaobject_list` setting has entries, render from it; otherwise render blocks.
- Shared snippets render both sources via params — never duplicate markup.
- Field names must match `docs/CONTENT-GUIDE.md` exactly. Do not invent fields.

## Metaobject types
- `meal_plan`, `how_it_works_step`, `faq_item`, `testimonial`, `delivery_zone`

## Product metafields (`custom`)
- `calories`, `protein`, `carbs`, `fat`, `ingredients`, `allergens`, `diet_tags`, `reheat_instructions`

## Coding standards
- Online Store 2.0, JSON templates, section presets with demo blocks.
- All merchant-facing strings via `locales/en.default.json` / `en.default.schema.json`.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, keyboard accordion, visible focus, alt text.
- Performance: `image_url` + `image_tag` with widths/sizes; lazy below fold; vanilla JS only.
- Prices only from product/variant: `{{ price | money }}`.
- Nil-safe Metaobject access; sort by `sort_order` / `step_number` when present.
- No apps, external services, or third-party scripts.
- Prefer scoped CSS in `assets/section-*.css` or `assets/prep-content.css`.
